module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.LineBundle.FibreCoordinate
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.RegularSectionCorrespondence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.GysinConstruction.ZeroScheme

/-!
# The zero scheme of the fibre coordinate is the zero scheme of the tautological section

The fibre coordinate `Stacks.LineBundle.fibreCoordinate` of the line bundle `L(M)` of an
invertible module `M` is a global section of `q^*M`, obtained from
`Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.tautologicalSection` — a global section of `(q^*(M^{⊗ -1}))^{⊗ -1}`
— by transporting it across the two dualization isomorphisms
`Stacks.ProjBundleInverseBaseChange.pullbackTensorPowerNegOneIso` and
`Stacks.PullbackTensorIso.tensorPowerNegOneNegOneIso`.

Both consumers that need the fibre coordinate's **zero scheme** —
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.AffineBundle.LineBundleChow`, which wants it identified with
the image of the zero section, and
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.TensorZeroScheme.Basic`, which wants it identified with a
coordinate hyperplane in a local presentation — recorded that the transport across those two
isomorphisms was the obstruction, neither being described on sections.

For the zero scheme the obstruction is not there: the defining ideal of
[Stacks, Tag 02OQ] is generated by the values of *all* the linear functionals on the sections of
the ambient module at the section, and an isomorphism of the ambient module is a bijection on
functionals carrying one generating set onto the other. That is
`AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme_eq_of_iso`, and applying it twice removes both dualization
isomorphisms from the problem at once: whatever either of them does to a section, it does not
move a zero scheme.

So the statement blocked at
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.AffineBundle.LineBundleChow` — that the zero scheme of the
fibre coordinate is the image of the zero section, which is part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0F96] — is
equivalent to the same statement for the tautological section of the situation `M^{⊗ -1}`, where
no dualization isomorphism appears and the section is the adjoint of the degree-one inclusion
`M^{⊗ -1} ⟶ Sym(M^{⊗ -1})`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LineBundle.zeroScheme_tautologicalSectionBase`: **the first dualization isomorphism
  does not move the zero scheme** — `Z(tautologicalSection) = Z(tautologicalSectionBase)`.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.zeroScheme_fibreCoordinate`: **the zero scheme of the fibre coordinate is
  the zero scheme of the tautological section**, both dualization isomorphisms removed.

## Implementation notes

The three ambient modules need their invertibility in the
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible` spelling, which is the one
`AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme` and `AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme_eq_of_iso` are stated over,
while what the construction of each supplies is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible`. The two are
transferred by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_iff_algebraicGeometry` and are declared here
as instances, since instance search does not cross between the spellings — the same discipline as
the spelling section of `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.LineBundle.FibreCoordinate`.

`Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.tautologicalSectionBase` and
`Stacks.LineBundle.fibreCoordinate` are defined with
`CategoryTheory.PresheafOfModules.Hom.app _ (Opposite.op ⊤)`, while
`AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme_eq_of_iso` hypothesizes
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.Hom.app _ ⊤`; the two agree by `rfl`, so each hypothesis is
discharged by `rfl` and no transport is needed.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F96](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F96)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CU)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite
open Stacks.SheafInternalHom (isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf)
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorPower (tensorPower isInvertible_tensorPower)

universe u

namespace Stacks.LineBundle

variable (D : Situation.{u})

/-- The module the tautological section lives in is invertible, in the
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible` spelling that the zero scheme is stated over. -/
instance isInvertible_pullbackInverse :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible D.totalSpace.sheaf.obj
      D.totalSpace.ringCatSheaf.property D.pullbackInverse :=
  (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_iff_algebraicGeometry _ _ _).mp
    (@isInvertible_tensorPower _ _ _ D.totalSpace.sheaf.obj
      D.totalSpace.ringCatSheaf.property _ _
      ((AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pullback D.totalSpaceToBase).obj D.L)
      D.isInvertible_stacks_pullback (-1))

/-- The pullback of the inverse is invertible, in the
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible` spelling. -/
instance isInvertible_basePullbackInverse :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible D.totalSpace.sheaf.obj
      D.totalSpace.ringCatSheaf.property D.basePullbackInverse :=
  haveI hL : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible D.X.presheaf
      (isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf D.X) D.L :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible.ofAlgebraicGeometry _ _ _ D.invertible
  haveI hP : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible D.X.presheaf
      (isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf D.X)
      (tensorPower D.X.presheaf (isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf D.X) D.L (-1)) :=
    @isInvertible_tensorPower _ _ _ D.X.presheaf (isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf D.X) _ _
      D.L hL (-1)
  (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_iff_algebraicGeometry _ _ _).mp
    (@Stacks.ProjBundleInverseBaseChange.isInvertible_pullbackFunctor_obj D.X D.totalSpace
      D.totalSpaceToBase
      (tensorPower D.X.presheaf (isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf D.X) D.L (-1)) hP)

/-- **The first dualization isomorphism does not move the zero scheme**: the zero scheme of the
tautological section, a section of `(q^*L)^{⊗ -1}`, is the zero scheme of the same section read
in `q^*(L^{⊗ -1})`. -/
theorem zeroScheme_tautologicalSectionBase :
    AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme D.totalSpace D.pullbackInverse D.tautologicalSection =
      AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme D.totalSpace D.basePullbackInverse
        D.tautologicalSectionBase :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme_eq_of_iso D.pullbackInverseIso rfl

variable (Y : Scheme.{u}) (M : Y.Modules)
  [hM : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible Y.sheaf.obj Y.ringCatSheaf.property M]

include hM in
/-- The pullback of `M` to the line bundle `L(M)` is invertible, in the
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible` spelling. -/
instance isInvertible_lineBundlePullback :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (lineBundleSpace Y M).sheaf.obj
      (lineBundleSpace Y M).ringCatSheaf.property (lineBundlePullback Y M) :=
  haveI : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible Y.presheaf (isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf Y) M :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible.ofAlgebraicGeometry _ _ _ hM
  (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_iff_algebraicGeometry _ _ _).mp
    (Stacks.ProjBundleInverseBaseChange.isInvertible_pullbackFunctor_obj
      (lineBundleProj Y M) M)

include hM in
/-- **The zero scheme of the fibre coordinate of `L(M)` is the zero scheme of the tautological
section of the situation `M^{⊗ -1}`.** Both dualization isomorphisms the fibre coordinate is
transported across are isomorphisms of the ambient invertible module, and the defining ideal of
the zero scheme of [Stacks, Tag 02OQ] is insensitive to those.

This is the reduction the identification of `Z(fibreCoordinate)` with the image of the zero
section — part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0F96] — was waiting on: the statement is now about the
tautological section alone. -/
theorem zeroScheme_fibreCoordinate :
    AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme (lineBundleSpace Y M) (lineBundlePullback Y M)
        (fibreCoordinate Y M) =
      AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme (inverseSituation Y M).totalSpace
        (inverseSituation Y M).pullbackInverse (inverseSituation Y M).tautologicalSection :=
  have : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible
      (inverseSituation Y M).totalSpace.sheaf.obj
      (inverseSituation Y M).totalSpace.ringCatSheaf.property (lineBundlePullback Y M) :=
    isInvertible_lineBundlePullback Y M
  ((zeroScheme_tautologicalSectionBase (inverseSituation Y M)).trans
    (AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme_eq_of_iso (lineBundlePullbackIso Y M) rfl)).symm

end Stacks.LineBundle

end
